<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/07/General-iCloud-App-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="160" height="90" class="brief" align="left" style="float:left;margin:0 20px 20px 0;width:160px;height:auto;" />Apple appears to have quietly tripled the number of iCloud Mail aliases users can create, increasing the limit from three to nine. The increase was first noticed last week by a <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/iCloud/comments/1wugvqz/did_the_icloud_email_alias_limit_increase_recently/">Reddit</a> user, and picked up shortly after by a member of the <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/aliases-increased-to-9.2490884/"><em>MacRumors</em> forums</a>. <em>MacRumors</em> can confirm the change is live at iCloud.com. <br/>
<br/>
